# d2decomped on PeOS (English)
# key=text, see peos/lang.h for the format.

nodata.title=The game's files are not here yet
nodata.1=Diablo II plays with your own copy of the game: the MPQ files
nodata.2=of Diablo II and Lord of Destruction, patch 1.14d. They go in
nodata.3=the folder /games/diablo2, on a PeOS installed on a disk
nodata.4=(about 2 GB: the live session cannot hold them).
nodata.5=To copy them, from a USB stick formatted as FAT32:
nodata.6=1. Put the files in a folder named diablo2 on the stick.
nodata.7=2. Plug it in and open Orbit:   mount usb /usb fat32
nodata.8=3. Then:   mkdir /games   and   cp -r /usb/diablo2 /games
nodata.9=The files: d2data, d2exp, d2char, d2sfx, d2speech, d2music,
nodata.10=d2xmusic, d2xtalk, d2video, d2xvideo and patch_d2 (.mpq).
nodata.ok=OK

# PeStore
store.summary=Diablo II and Lord of Destruction, with your own copy of the game.
store.description=d2decomped, a reimplementation of Diablo II and Lord of Destruction (1.14d), on PeOS. It plays with your own game files: make the data disk with the tool at github.com/teddi201252/peos-d2d (Windows, macOS, Linux), attach it and mount it on /games/diablo2.\nThe source of this app is there too (GPL-3.0). Not affiliated with Blizzard Entertainment.
